    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are leaning heavily into speed and top-of-the-order efficiency today, led by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98), who registers as our premier start. His matchup against Pfaadt is ideal, but the true differentiator is the \"Slow SP Delivery\" factor, which projectable data suggests offers a massive green light for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** to secure a stolen base, our scarcest category. **Junior Caminero** (74.78) and **Yordan Alvarez** (73.61) provide elite middle-order production, with **Yordan Alvarez** specifically benefiting from an elite .458 xwOBA that remains impervious to most matchup variables. While **Kyle Schwarber** (60.24) and **Trea Turner** (61.16) face a tough test against Kirby, their roles at the top of the lineup keep them firmly in our starting rotation despite the neutral-to-negative park factors.\n\nStrategic benching remains critical to our game-cap management, with **Carson Benge** (36.49) representing our most difficult exclusion. While his projected usage as a #3 hitter is enticing, the combination of a sharp drop in park-adjusted efficiency and the unfavorable matchup against Harrison\u2014who boasts a 3.05 xERA\u2014tipped the optimizer to bench him rather than risk a sub-40 performance. Similarly, **Chase Meidroth** (34.95) was disqualified due to the formidable presence of deGrom, whose elite SP skill acts as a significant suppressor for hitters with less established track records. \n\nWe are monitoring the risk profile of **Gary Sanchez** (57.19) and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (53.68); both are currently slotted into the lineup, but their scores sit near our \"Marginal\" threshold. Should weather reports or late-scratch notifications emerge, we are prepared to pivot to our depth, though for now, the platoon advantages for both players against Thornton and Liberatore respectively justify their inclusion. With **Christian Yelich** and **Colt Keith** currently unavailable, we will rely on the consistency of **Lars Nootbaar** (62.07), whose platoon edge against Holmes provides a stable floor for our outfield.",
